{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For the way was blocked (yarat) before me — for.</b> Ki has the sense of 'even,' as in 'כי מנשה הבכור רפאה נפשי כי חטאתי לך' — even Menasheh the firstborn, heal my soul, for I have sinned against You." "<b>Yarat.</b> A term of blocking, as in 'יסגירנו אל אל עויל' and 'וע״י רשעים ירטני' — through the wicked he blocks me. Thus the interpretation: behold, I went out to be an adversary to you, and even though the way was blocked before me."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:20.629984780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}